%[text] # Method: `solve2PortNetwork`
%[text] JVsound, J.G. Vermond
disp(datetime("today")) %[output:7e97dd73]
%[text] ## Description
%[text] The method `solve2PortNetwork` resides in the class `lspsys`. It combines all transmission matrices for the system and solves it for volume velocity created by the driver's diaphragm.
%[text] Syntax:
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] val = obj.solve2PortNetwork
%[text] ```
%[text] ```
%[text] val = struct with fields:
%[text] 
%[text] DiaphragmVolumeVelocity   Diaphragm volume velocity [m^3/s]
%[text] SourceCurrent   Electric current [A]
%[text] ```
%[text] The 2-port network matrices are of the ABCD or transmission parameters type, see the image and equation below.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![](text:image:0313)
%[text] $\\left\[ \\matrix{ \nV\_1 \\cr\ni\_2 }\n\\right\] \n=\n\\left\[ \\matrix{\nA & B \\cr\nC & D }\n\\right\]\n\\left\[ \\matrix{\nV\_2 \\cr\ni\_2 }\n\\right\]\n$
%[text] ## Equivalent electrical circuit
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![](text:image:731e)
%[text] 

